  "content": {
    "id": "p20-q31-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "31",
    "prompt": "The iconic soccer ball design consists of $P$ pentagons and $H$ hexagons sewn together to form a polyhedron. Let $V$, $E$ and $F$ denote the number of vertices, edges and faces in the polyhedron.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p20-q31-diagram",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "image",
        "code": null,
        "src": "/booklet-assets/enrichment-maths-1-part12-20261008/source-soccer-ball.png",
        "widthMm": 65,
        "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
        "overlayOf": null,
        "transparent": false,
        "axes": null,
        "retentionReason": "Isolated original soccer-ball panel network. Pentagons and hexagons, black/white panels and perspective adjacency are mathematically relevant; preserve the original photograph rather than risk an unverified reconstruction.",
        "derived": false
      }
    ],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p20-q31-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Determine $F$ in terms of $P$ and $H$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$F=P+H$.",
          "worked": "Each pentagon and each hexagon contributes one face.\n$$F=P+H.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q31-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Determine $E$ in terms of $P$ and $H$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$E=\\dfrac{5P+6H}{2}$.\n\nEach edge belongs to two faces.",
          "worked": "The faces have $5P+6H$ sides altogether. Each edge is counted twice, once for each adjoining face.\n$$\\begin{align*}2E&=5P+6H\\\\E&=\\frac{5P+6H}{2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q31-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Determine $V$ in terms of $P$ and $H$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$V=\\dfrac{5P+6H}{3}$.\n\nThree faces meet at each vertex.",
          "worked": "One pentagon and two hexagons meet at each vertex. Counting the corners of all faces therefore counts each vertex three times.\n$$\\begin{align*}3V&=5P+6H\\\\V&=\\frac{5P+6H}{3}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q31-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Determine $V-E+F$ in terms of $P$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$V-E+F=\\dfrac{P}{6}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}V-E+F&=\\frac{5P+6H}{3}-\\frac{5P+6H}{2}+P+H\\\\V-E+F&=\\frac{2(5P+6H)-3(5P+6H)+6P+6H}{6}\\\\V-E+F&=\\frac{P}{6}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q31-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "Hence, determine $P$ and $H$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P=12$, $H=20$.\n\nUse Euler's formula, then count one pentagon corner and two hexagon corners at each vertex.",
          "worked": "Euler's formula gives $V-E+F=2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{P}{6}&=2\\\\P&=12.\\end{align*}$$\nEach vertex belongs to one pentagon and two hexagons, so the number of hexagon corners is twice the number of pentagon corners.\n$$\\begin{align*}6H&=2(5P)\\\\6H&=2(5\\times12)\\\\6H&=120\\\\H&=20.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 76
      }
    ]
  },
